# synapse_fbs C headers

Generated with flatcc {{ flatcc_version }}. Reflection schemas generated with
flatc {{ flatbuffers_version }} are included under `bfbs/`. The archive also
ships `topics.json` and `include/synapse/topic_catalog.h` for canonical Zenoh
keys, `TopicId`, root table names, and payload types.

This archive is a generic CMake dependency and also carries a
`zephyr/module.yml`, so it can be used with CMake `find_package`,
`FetchContent`, or as a Zephyr module from a west manifest. Link
`synapse_fbs::c` for reader-only accessors.

Prefer `find_package` when the archive is downloaded, extracted, or installed
outside the project configure step:

```cmake
find_package(synapse_fbs {{ package_version }} CONFIG REQUIRED)

target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE synapse_fbs::c)
```

Set `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` to the extracted archive root, for example
`/path/to/synapse_fbs-c`.

Use `FetchContent` when the project should fetch the GitHub Release archive
directly:

```cmake
include(FetchContent)

FetchContent_Declare(
  synapse_fbs
  URL https://github.com/CogniPilot/synapse_fbs/releases/download/{{ release_name }}/synapse_fbs-c.tar.gz
  URL_HASH SHA256=<release sha256>
  DOWNLOAD_EXTRACT_TIMESTAMP TRUE
)
FetchContent_MakeAvailable(synapse_fbs)

target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE synapse_fbs::c)
```

Link `synapse_fbs::flatcc_runtime` when using generated builders, verifiers, or
JSON helpers.

Link `synapse_fbs::cdr`, or enable `CONFIG_SYNAPSE_FBS_CDR` when the archive is
loaded as a Zephyr module, for the allocation-free little-endian CDRv1 codecs
and generated projection catalog. The application selects publishers, ROS
topics, Zenoh routes, QoS, and traffic policy.

```c
#include <synapse/topic_catalog.h>

const synapse_topic_info_t *topic = synapse_topic_by_key("vehicle_health");
```

Link `synapse_fbs::mcap`, or enable `CONFIG_SYNAPSE_FBS_MCAP` when the archive
is loaded as a Zephyr module, for the allocation-free `synapse/1` streaming
writer. The application explicitly declares each logged topic and owns the
queue, output buffer, thread, and storage sink.
